WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:10.798
The next day Raoul was still doubting what he'd seen and heard in Christine's dressing room. "Did I really

2
00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:18.697
hear a man singing?" he asked himself. "I'm sure I did, but there was no one there other

3
00:00:18.698 --> 00:00:24.702
than Christine . . . and then she vanished through the mirror!" He decided to pay a call on

4
00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:35.696
Mama Valerius in the hope that Christine had contacted her. When Raoul arrived at the old woman's apartment,

5
00:00:35.758 --> 00:00:41.951
he was astonished to find Christine herself. She was seated by the bed of Mama Valerius, who was sitting

6
00:00:41.952 --> 00:00:48.090
up and knitting. The color had returned to Christine's cheeks, and there were no longer shadows under her eyes.

7
00:00:48.091 --> 00:00:53.309
Without showing any emotion, Christine rose and held out her hands to Raoul. But he was so flabbergasted

8
00:00:54.539 --> 00:01:08.978
by her reappearance that he was speechless. Mama Valerius laughed. "Don't you recognize our Christine? Her Angel of Music

9
00:01:09.095 --> 00:01:15.097
has returned her to us after two long weeks." "Mama, you know there's no such thing as the

10
00:01:15.098 --> 00:01:24.459
Angel of Music!" Christine scolded. Raoul sensed that Christine didn't want Mama Valerius to talk about the angel in

11
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:38.093
front of him, but Mama Valerius didn't take the hint. "But, child, he's been giving you lessons—" "Mama, I've

12
00:01:38.094 --> 00:01:45.033
promised to explain everything someday. Until that day comes, please promise you won't ask any more questions." "I

13
00:01:45.034 --> 00:01:53.393
will, provided you promise never to leave me again. Can you do that, Christine?" The younger woman glanced nervously

14
00:01:53.394 --> 00:02:01.521
at Raoul and sat down. "Mama, none of this can be of interest to Monsieur de Chagny." "On

15
00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:13.702
the contrary, mademoiselle, I am very interested," Raoul said, taking a seat in a chair next to her. "After

16
00:02:13.703 --> 00:02:21.151
what happened last night, I'm delighted—and surprised—to find you here. As an old friend, I'm concerned that your

17
00:02:21.152 --> 00:02:29.983
secrecy may prove fatal to you." Mama Valerius gasped and dropped a knitting needle. "Is Christine in danger?" Without

18
00:02:29.984 --> 00:02:37.557
waiting for an answer, she said, "Christine, you must tell me everything right now! And what is this danger,

19
00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:44.610
Monsieur de Chagny?" "There is a terrible mystery surrounding Christine and the opera house, a mystery more frightening

20
00:02:44.611 --> 00:02:50.642
than any ghost. I believe an imposter is pretending to be the Angel of Music to take advantage of

21
00:02:50.643 --> 00:03:00.545
Christine." Christine put a protective arm around Mama Valerius. "Don't believe him!" "You must promise never to leave

22
00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:12.137
me again." Mama Valerius patted Christine's arm, but the young woman remained silent. "That's the only thing that can

23
00:03:12.138 --> 00:03:20.147
reassure the two of us," Raoul added. "We won't question you about the past, if you remain under our

24
00:03:20.148 --> 00:03:26.852
protection in the future." But Christine refused to make any promises. "You have no right to control my

25
00:03:26.853 --> 00:03:34.408
actions, Monsieur de Chagny. As for the past two weeks, there's only one person who could question me about

26
00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:41.018
that: my husband. Well, I have no husband, and I never intend to marry, so I don't have

27
00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:47.451
to listen to anybody, especially you!" As she gestured wildly, Raoul was alarmed to notice a plain gold ring

28
00:03:47.452 --> 00:03:53.405
on her left hand. Raoul tried to grab her hand. "You have no husband, and yet you wear a

29
00:03:54.174 --> 00:04:03.251
wedding ring!" "That's a present!" Christine blushed as she hid her hand behind her back. "Since you have

30
00:04:03.252 --> 00:04:08.642
no husband, that ring can only have been given by someone who hopes to be your husband! Are you

31
00:04:08.643 --> 00:04:19.698
engaged?" Raoul asked. "That's none of your business," Christine said. "As far as I'm concerned—" "I beg your

32
00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:25.150
pardon, mademoiselle." Raoul interrupted for fear she was about to banish him forever. "I have sometimes doubted the evidence

33
00:04:25.151 --> 00:04:32.241
I've seen with my own eyes." "Well, what did you think you saw?" Christine was angry now. "I saw

34
00:04:32.365 --> 00:04:40.672
your joy at the sound of a man's voice coming from a wall in your dressing room. Your

35
00:04:40.728 --> 00:04:50.483
joy ," Raoul repeated for emphasis. "You've spoken about the Angel of Music and then tell us today that

36
00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:57.237
there is no such thing. In that case, why did you look as radiant as if you were

37
00:04:57.238 --> 00:05:04.438
really hearing angels? Why did you follow the voice through the mirror?" "What is he talking about?" Mama Valerius

38
00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:09.723
looked concerned. Christine stayed silent while Raoul went on. "You're under a very dangerous spell. I myself was so

39
00:05:09.724 --> 00:05:16.318
enchanted by the voice that you vanished before my eyes. Tell us the name of the man behind

40
00:05:16.319 --> 00:05:19.826
the voice—the man who dares to put a ring on your finger!" "I'll never tell you!" Christine said. Hearing

41
00:05:19.827 --> 00:05:25.668
the way that Christine talked to Raoul, Mama Valerius suddenly took her side. "Monsieur de Chagny, if Christine

42
00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:32.241
loves that man, what business is it of yours?" Tears filled Raoul's eyes. "Alas, madame, I believe that Christine

43
00:05:32.242 --> 00:05:41.602
really does love him, even though he is not worthy of her love. She may not want to identify

44
00:05:41.603 --> 00:05:48.145
him, but at least I know his first name is Erik." Startled by this revelation, Christine turned white.

45
00:05:48.245 --> 00:05:55.526
"What? Who told you that?" "You did." "I never said his name," Christine insisted. "What are you talking about?"

46
00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:04.253
"You were pitying him last night. When you entered your dressing room, you said, 'Poor Erik.' Well, poor

47
00:06:04.254 --> 00:06:13.405
Raoul overheard you." Christine was furious now. "This is the second time you've stood outside my dressing room—my private

48
00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:24.655
dressing room—and listened through the door." "I wasn't outside in the passage, Christine. I was in your dressing

49
00:06:24.656 --> 00:06:32.017
room behind the curtain." "Oh, you miserable man!" Christine moaned while her face showed every sign of unspeakable terror.

50
00:06:32.018 --> 00:06:43.167
"You're going to get yourself killed." "If that's what happens, so be it, but I must protect you from

51
00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:50.776
this evil man." Raoul said these words with so much love and despair that Christine could not hold

52
00:06:50.777 --> 00:07:02.654
back a sob. She took his hands and looked at him with all the affection she felt for him.

53
00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:12.659
"Raoul, forget the man's voice and his name. You must never try to solve any mystery connected to

54
00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:20.528
that voice." "Is the mystery so very terrible?" "There is no more awful mystery on earth. Promise me that

55
00:07:20.529 --> 00:07:34.004
you will make no attempt to learn anything more about the voice or the man. And promise me that

56
00:07:34.005 --> 00:07:43.391
you will never come to my dressing room unless I invite you." Raoul feared that Christine would never

57
00:07:43.392 --> 00:07:50.625
extend that invitation. "Do you promise to send for me, Christine?" "I promise." But that was not enough for

58
00:07:50.626 --> 00:07:58.072
Raoul. "When?" he demanded. "Tomorrow," Christine replied. "Then I will do as you ask." Raoul kissed Christine's hands

59
00:07:58.073 --> 00:08:05.654
and said farewell to Mama Valerius. Outside on the sidewalk, he muttered Erik's name and vowed to be patient.

